docs/context/decision_log.md:682:     - Renders: `docs/renders/2026-10-22-calling/round-1/storyboard-A-reserved.png`, `storyboard-B-current.png`.
docs/context/decision_log.md:683:  16. **Update 2026-10-24 — case page layout (Apurva):** **Order details always first**; directly under it **one slot for "what to say / what happened"** — the script during the call, then the outcome card in the same place once the case closes (replaces "status card on top" from the approved closed screens). The script card has **one title, "End-of-call script"** (the separate "Call" title is dropped — the card holds only the script since D-28 moved the buttons to the bar).
docs/context/decision_log.md:684:  17. **Update 2026-10-24 — what happened vs what to say (Apurva):** two cards with two jobs, stacked in the slot under Order details: the **outcome card** says what happened ("Forwarded to HA"; **amber** with "The HA couldn't join." when a transfer fails), and the **End-of-call script** card says what to say ("Our Health Advisor will call you shortly."). The script card always looks the same (never amber) so doctors recognise it; amber belongs to the event. Replaces the "line inside the outcome card" in point 15.
docs/context/decision_log.md:685:  18. **Update 2026-10-24 (Apurva):** **Callback during the call in all cases** — the bar is the same during every call ("Calling {name}…" + Callback). **The End-of-call script shows from the tap on Call patient** until the call ends, in the slot under Order details (the D-55 rule that the Call card sits above the medicines while the call is live still applies). Unavailable keeps the approved destructive style (red outline, phone-off icon). Full draft: `docs/renders/2026-10-22-calling/storyboard-all-states.png` (states in `round-2/`, local).
docs/context/decision_log.md:686:  19. **Update 2026-10-24 (Apurva, agreed with Engineering):** the app gets the call status by **polling** the backend while a call is active (Engineering sets the interval; ~3 s discussed), with an immediate check when the doctor returns to the screen; it stops at the outcome. Engineering implements it in **both the current web portal and the new app**, so both behave the same (no GTM split). Answers the method part of OQ-030.
docs/context/decision_log.md:687:  20. **Update 2026-10-24 — no call result (state 7), Apurva:** replaces the earlier "result not received" rule. **Release (Back) is decided:** before an attempted call, Back opens "Leave this case?" and Release returns the case to the queue immediately; Back also shows during "Calling…" (7a, 7b). **At 3 minutes with no result** (backend timer, repeats every 3 min) the bar asks **"Are you still on the call?"** · Yes, still talking / No, call ended. "No" is the active trigger for the backend's fallback check with the partner; if nothing comes back: **"We didn't get the call result."** · **Confirm prescription** · Callback · Unavailable (no Back — the attempt must be recorded). Confirm here shows a grey **"Prescription submitted — It will be confirmed once we receive the call record."** card; the backend confirms when the record arrives (50 s or more); a record that never arrives goes to the Ops review queue (OQ-033); a late record showing under 50 s or no answer is to be decided separately. No Confirm is ever shown on a timer at 50 s without proof. A result at any point goes straight to its outcome. Rejected: patient verification code, short re-call, ops-only route, daily cap and declaration sheet (too complex), Call again in 7d (Callback covers it). Storyboard: `docs/renders/2026-10-22-calling/storyboard-state-7.png`.
docs/context/decision_log.md:688:  21. **Update 2026-10-24 — End-of-call scripts (Apurva):** before the tap, "I'm writing your prescription now…" + the next step (Cat4: track your order in the Truemeds app · transfer: stay on the line, I'll connect you to our Health Advisor · forward: our Health Advisor will call you shortly · fallback B: …will help you with the next steps). After the tap, when no HA is free or the transfer fails: card "Forwarded to HA · HA unavailable right now." and script "I've written your prescription. Our Health Advisor isn't available right now — they'll call you back shortly." Same verb ("write"), tense follows the moment; "Health Advisor" spelled out for the patient, "HA" only on the doctor's card. Copy keys `call.script*`, `call.forwardedTell`, `call.transferFailed`.
docs/context/decision_log.md:690:  22. **Update 2026-10-24 — dropped calls: talk time adds up (Apurva, option A):** the 50-second gate counts the **total connected talk time across calls on the same case**, not one call. Guards (settings; starting values for Engineering): only connected calls of **at least ~10 s** count; only calls on the same case **within ~30 min** count together. The doctor is never shown the maths — state 6 says "Call too short to write a prescription. Call again to continue." Also settles a submitted case whose late record shows under 50 s: it is judged on the total. Answers OQ-001. Rejected: a shorter second-call gate (two numbers, arbitrary); keeping every call at 50 s (today's frustration).
docs/context/decision_log.md:691:  23. **Update 2026-10-24 — final review fixes (Apurva):** (1) **State 6 drops Unavailable** — the patient did pick up; Call again finds out, and an unanswered call closes as unavailable automatically: **Call again · Callback**. (2) **"Health Advisor" spelled out everywhere** (cards, notices, scripts) — "HA" no longer shown to the doctor. (3) **State 16 names who ended the call** when the backend knows (Ozonetel `HANGUP` = doctor, `DIAL` = patient, or CDR `Comments`): doctor → "You ended the call before the transfer. Next time, stay on the line until the Health Advisor joins…"; patient → "The patient ended the call before the transfer…"; unknown → neutral. (4) **15 and B3 tell the doctor to end the call**: "…Read the script, then end the call."
docs/context/decision_log.md:692:  24. **Update 2026-10-25 — round-4 review (Apurva):** (1) **Callback in every live call until the doctor taps a confirm button** — none in 13 Transferring, B2 Checking for a Health Advisor, or the 7b question; added to 17 (Skip HA, waiting). (2) **Script hidden on 8a/8b** — the result arrives only after the call has ended; kept on 12 (transfer, call live). (3) **Skip HA shown after a missed transfer** (16, 16b, 16c) — "no other conditions" applies. (4) **15 and B3 stay as they are**: closed card + "Read the script, then end the call" + Request next case. Already decided, docs corrected: Cat4 script (point 21), no Unavailable on 6 (23), Confirm on 7d (20), Skip HA during a transfer call waits for the result (14). Rebuild items logged: labels typed inline in the render recipes (use `MSG()`); closed/after-confirm states must render View Rx, medicines and notes read-only.
docs/context/decision_log.md:693:  25. **Update 2026-10-25 — round-5 answers (Apurva):** t17 (Skip HA during a live transfer call) **keeps the script** — the call is live; point 24-2 only hides it once the call has ended. No Callback on 7b, 13 and B2 confirmed as intended exceptions.
