docs/context/decision_log.md:721:- **Update 2026-10-25 (Apurva, after a one-screen experiment — `docs/renders/2026-10-25-card-tray-experiment/`):** (4) **Card look = C5**: tint + 1px edge in the tone colour, no drop shadow. Neutral keeps a **grey-100 fill** with a grey-200 edge (grey-50 is the page colour; grey-200 reads disabled). Rejected: tint only (success too pale on the grey page), left accent bar (weak, bends at the corner), border only (looks like a selected field — same problem as 7b), white card with icon chip (looks like content). (5) **Bottom action bar = T3**: hairline top edge + soft upward shadow; SALT's shadow points down, so the bar merged with white cards. Rejected: upward shadow only (soft), grey bar (reads disabled, buttons compete). (6) 7b question shown as plain text, no box. (8) **Tray depth = option B** (Apurva, 2026-10-26): same hairline and shape, deeper upward shadow (0 -8px 24px, 10%). Rejected: side shadows (a full-width bar has no sides to cast from), floating bar with margins (breaks the 7b pair at 360, content shows around it, reads as a half-open sheet), square corners (no gain). `exp-tray-shape-w360.png`. (7) **B3 is amber, like 15** (Apurva, 2026-10-26): same outcome and same action for the doctor (forwarded, read the script, end the call); amber = done but you still have to act. Replaces the earlier green. Research: Polaris / Atlassian / Material 3 tint + icon for status; iOS / Material bars use an edge or upward shadow.
