docs/context/decision_log.md:873:### D-82 · Fix round closed (Rounds 1–6); design-system standards; screens frozen again — 2026-11-03
docs/context/decision_log.md:874:- **Decision (Apurva):** the fix round (`docs/renders/2026-11-01-fix-round/`, Rounds 1–6, report `REPORT.md`) is accepted and the screens and app logic are **frozen again**, now covering D-01 → D-82 (145 states, 390 and 360). It applied D-80 and D-81, plus:
docs/context/decision_log.md:887:### D-83 · Calling walkthrough decisions (CW-A1 … CW-F3) — 2026-11-03
docs/context/decision_log.md:888:- **Decision (Apurva):** her misses from the calling walkthrough were reviewed path by path and decided in `docs/reviews/2026-11-02-calling-walkthrough/README.md` (full reasons and rejected options there). Applied to the frozen screens by the calling round (`docs/renders/2026-11-03-calling-round/`). Latest wins over D-58, D-63, D-75 pt 3 and D-81 F26 where named.
docs/context/decision_log.md:903:### D-84 · Copy standard adopted; copy fixes go to a PRD annex, not to the frozen pictures — 2026-11-03
docs/context/decision_log.md:905:  1. **Copy rules v2** (`docs/reviews/2026-11-03-copy-audit/COPY-RULES.md`, 26 rules) are the standard for all app text. They were drafted from D-48 / D-65 / D-66 / D-77 / D-81 / D-83, checked against the Atlassian, Polaris, Apple HIG and Material writing guides, and revised after a Codex critique (`codex-report.md`). Pointer in `docs/feedback-rules.md` §11.
docs/context/decision_log.md:910:- **Main-thread calls on the copy round's questions (Apurva delegated, 09:45):** outcome lines are fixed in the case page's relabel layer (`case.html`), not in the old prototype's `app.js`; "shortly" dropped from the forward scripts (no agreed callback time — rule 6); "Unavailable" kept as a fixed button name; timers stay "m:ss"; "Wrong code." and "Your selection is saved." kept (D-81 / D-65); "Not you? Switch account" kept (one button); no new screen for a missing record (D-83 pt 9: the doctor isn't interrupted; s7f says "It isn't confirmed until the call record arrives."); "Our Ops team" stays a placeholder (OQ-035); hidden legacy markup in `case.html` left for the rebuild; accessibility items F24–F26, F28 moved to the prototype build (backlog). Rules → v2.1.
docs/context/decision_log.md:913:### D-85 · Skip HA on a live call: one waiting screen, confirm on the result (17 changed) — 2026-11-03
docs/context/decision_log.md:919:- **Still open in the readiness thread:** answered 2026-11-03 — see D-87.
docs/context/decision_log.md:921:### D-86 · The notice band inside the action bar is centred — 2026-11-03
docs/context/decision_log.md:922:- **Decision (Apurva, after a side-by-side render, `docs/reviews/2026-11-03-copy-audit/bar-notice-alignment.png`):** the result notice inside the pinned bar (`.tm-actionbar > .tm-notice`, D-82) is centred: icon and text centred as a group, wrapped lines centred and balanced. All other notices (top of the page, inside sheets, in content) stay left-aligned.
docs/context/decision_log.md:924:- **Applied:** one central CSS rule, RULES §9.5, beyond-salt, re-render of the states with a band in the bar (`docs/renders/2026-11-03-bar-notice-centre/`), then the Design System artifact.
docs/context/decision_log.md:926:### D-87 · Fallback B is the one Pilot flow; A-only screens later; calling-flow page for Engineering — 2026-11-03
docs/context/decision_log.md:930:  3. **Calling-flow page** for Engineering (`calling-flow/`, live on the doctor-portal site at `/calling-flow/`): every calling state, trigger, button, event and rule from app-logic; solid = doctor action, dashed = backend event; **happy path** per case type (Cat4 / HA skipped → 10a; Pilot → 14 Transferred, not the forward) drawn blue, happy-path boxes filled (primary), others white (secondary); highlighting a case type numbers its happy path with Previous / Next. Checklist and results `docs/reviews/2026-11-03-calling-flow-site/CHECKLIST.md`.
docs/context/decision_log.md:934:### D-88 · Build readiness answered: v3 now, shell first; Part C closed; deploy on request; Help / bell placeholder — 2026-11-05
docs/context/decision_log.md:943:### D-89 · Pilot 7d ends on Forwarded; phone check at step 6; testing on a phone — 2026-11-05
docs/context/decision_log.md:947:  3. **Testing on a phone** (clarified 2026-11-06: covers every journey — sign-in, OTP, unlock, Home, case, Prescribe and calling — and the drawer shows the controls for the current screen): the phone shows only the app. The story is set on the desktop review panel and sent by **QR code / play link** (no server); a small **hidden drawer** on the phone changes things mid-flow. A **live desktop remote** is a later option (backlog §4b).
docs/context/decision_log.md:951:### D-90 · Build plan and rebuild checklist v3.2 approved; build starts at step 0 — 2026-11-06
docs/context/decision_log.md:952:- **Decision (Apurva):** `docs/proposals/2026-11-05-prototype-build-plan-v3.md` and `docs/reviews/2026-11-05-rebuild-checklist-v3.md` (v3.2, incl. D-88, D-89 and the independent review merged in `docs/reviews/2026-11-05-plan-v3-review/MERGE.md`) approved as the definition of done for the prototype build. P1–P6 as written. Build starts at step 0 (shell + the stale-line fixes in MERGE.md §4). Frozen from here: new findings are bugs or next-version ideas.
docs/context/decision_log.md:953:- Also done before approval: `a-confirm-failed` re-rendered without Callback (D-83 CW-C3; bug, backlog 2026-11-05).
docs/context/decision_log.md:956:### D-91 · 7c "Checking call result" shows the same screen as 5 — 2026-11-06
docs/context/decision_log.md:961:### D-92 · Sample doctor is "Dr. Kunal" (unlock greeting, Profile) — 2026-11-06
docs/context/decision_log.md:962:- **Decision (Apurva):** the sample doctor is **Dr. Kunal** — the returning-unlock greeting reads "Hello, Dr. Kunal" (was "Hello, Dr. Apurva") and the Profile page shows "Dr. Kunal Wani" with initials "KW" (was "Dr. Apurva Shetty", "AS"; Dr. Kunal Wani, Truemeds COO, who agreed (Apurva, 2026-11-06)). Re-rendered: returning-unlock (7 states) and the Home Profile pictures (3 states), 390 / 360; nothing else on them changes.
docs/context/decision_log.md:965:- **Restored 2026-11-09** from the build thread's chat after the old Mac died before this entry was committed; the re-rendered pictures were lost too and are redone in the step 1 recovery round.
docs/context/decision_log.md:967:### D-93 · Faster sign-in offer: the phone can't do it at Turn on — 2026-11-09 (placement revised the same day)
docs/context/decision_log.md:968:- **Decision (Apurva):** if the phone answers "unavailable" when the doctor taps **Turn on** (e.g. fingerprints removed after the offer appeared), the offer screen **stays as it was**: title, subtitle, tile and the three points. The bar shows an **amber warning notice** ("Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now.", `unlock.unavailable`, `alert-triangle`) above a single primary **Continue** → Home. Not now is hidden. Faster sign-in is not enabled, and the offer is recorded as shown. New state `offer_unavailable` (390 / 360), plus one new label "Continue" (`offer.continue`). Approved concept: `docs/renders/2026-11-09-step1-recovery/session-5/d93/bar-proposal/`. Closes OQ-036.
docs/context/decision_log.md:970:- **Rejected:** notice at the top of the panel (first D-93 version, rendered in session 5: that placement is for the screen's general situation, not the result of a tap); hiding the three points; a bottom sheet (sheets are for choices and confirmations, RULES §9.4, and a one-button sheet is just an alert); Try again (can't succeed); going to Home silently; "Biometrics is not enabled" (wrong in two of the three causes, and jargon); opening phone settings now (iOS can't open the Face ID / Touch ID page, and the web prototype can't open settings at all). Android "Set up on this phone" is logged in backlog §4b.
docs/context/decision_log.md:972:### D-94 · Approved pictures re-rendered on the new Mac (same designs) — 2026-11-09
docs/context/decision_log.md:977:### D-96 · Native hand-off kit for the React Native team, piloted on Sign-in — 2026-11-09
docs/context/decision_log.md:978:- **Decision (Apurva):** the React Native team gets a **hand-off kit** in the repo (`handoff/`), not a token list or hand-written RN code. For people: foundation files (tokens, icons, messages, native fonts), a spec for each building block (parts × states → native token), a screen viewer (tap an element → block, tokens, spacing; "tokens used" table; raw values flagged red), behaviour links and a "what changed" list. For their AI: `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md`, a skill, one data file per screen, and `DECIDED.md` / `OPEN.md`. Everything factual is generated from files we already maintain. (1) The app team builds and owns the RN components and screens; we own the contract. (2) The October TSX and hand-off notes in `ui-screens/native/` are marked "don't use — see `handoff/`" once the kit is approved (backlog). (3) Pilot screen: Sign-in. Proposal: `docs/proposals/2026-11-09-native-handoff-kit.md` (§6 is the done-checklist). **Amended same day (Apurva):** built the D-95 fast-build way: Codex writes the checks from the proposal before the build and is the fresh-AI tester and the critic; tap-to-inspect at 390 only (360 as pictures); one evidence sheet; runs in parallel with the prototype build (own files only). (Numbered D-96: D-95 is the fast build.)
docs/context/decision_log.md:982:### D-95 · Fast build for steps 2–8: lift the approved HTML, test the logic, picture compare as a report — 2026-11-09
docs/context/decision_log.md:983:- **Decision (Apurva):** steps 2–8 are built in two terminal runs (A: steps 2–5, B: steps 6–8), aiming to finish today. The approved, audited HTML for every state is lifted into the app. The plan v3.2 build rules (B1–B14) stay. **Cut:** the per-state pixel gate (the compare runs once per run as a report, and only states over 1% different are looked at); per-session Codex loops. Instead, per run, **Codex writes the test cases and Playwright tests from the spec before the build**, and does one full critique at the end (Apurva: use Codex fully; tests written independently of the build); per-state tests for screens that only display (tests stay for gates, routing, outcomes, hold / retry, refusals, reopen); per-session screenshots. Brief: `docs/renders/2026-11-09-build-fast/TERMINAL-BRIEF.md`. Amends D-90 (plan v3.2 §5 and B15) for steps 2–8.
docs/context/decision_log.md:989:### D-60 · Secondary button without drop shadow (design system) — 2026-10-24 · **REVERTED same day**
docs/context/decision_log.md:990:- **Reverted (Apurva, 2026-10-24):** keep the secondary button as SALT has it today — white, grey border, brand label, drop shadow. The change below was undone; recorded so it isn't proposed again without new information.
docs/context/decision_log.md:994:- Render: `docs/renders/2026-10-22-calling/secondary-shadow-before-after.png`. Affects every screen with a secondary button (approved A–D renders show the old shadow until re-rendered).
